course: dictionary
lesson: 3073
title: One word, many meanings: edge
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word edge can mean more than one thing. The context tells you which meaning is right. In «The satanic leaf-tailed gecko has a body and tail that look like a dry curled leaf with nibbled edges», edges are the outside lines of the tail, not a cliff or a table.
explain: Edge can also be a verb. To edge means to move slowly and carefully. If a sentence says someone edged closer to the door, picture them moving very quietly and carefully, not running. Ask: does the word fit the action in the sentence?
explain: In maths, the edge of a solid shape is the line where two faces meet. A cube has 12 edges, so you can count them to check. In safety, «stay away from the edge» means keep well back from the drop. «On edge» is different again: it means nervous, not near a border.
fact: An edge is the outside line or end of something, like the edge of a table or a cliff.
fact: The edge of a solid shape is the line where two faces meet. A cube has 12 edges.
fact: The edge of a knife is its sharp side.
fact: To edge means to move slowly and carefully.
fact: «On edge» means nervous. It is an idiom, so do not read it word by word.
exercise: «Stay away from the edge of the platform.» What does edge mean here? | The middle of a train | The inside of the station | The sharp side of a knife | *The outside end or border
exercise: «Male emperor penguins huddle in thousands, taking turns at the cold edge.» What is the cold edge? | The middle of the huddle, where it is warmest | *The outside of the huddle, where it is coldest | The eggs on their feet | The sea under the ice
exercise: How many edges does a cube have? | 8 | 4 | 6 | *12
test: «She breaks off a bit of the edge with each hand.» What is the edge of this object? | The outside border or rim | The middle of the object | The crack in the middle | *The part of the object that is broken off, its outside border
test: Ben wants to edge closer to the frog without scaring it. What does edge mean? | To shout loudly | To close the door | *To move slowly and carefully | To jump quickly
exam: «Heat milk and a skin forms on top, until the milk suddenly rushes over the edge of the pan.» What does edge mean here? | *The top rim, the border where the pan ends | The handle of the pan | The sharp side of a knife | The bottom of the pan
